SliceViewport.description:
Where a full-viewport slice video sits (`SliceVideo.viewport`, owner 2026-10-01). The slice then fills the whole viewport (its whole width, the screen's height) instead of the reading column, and the video – and its poster – is placed in that box (owner 2026-10-01, four fits):
- `contain` "Ganz sichtbar" / "Show all" (the default): the whole video, as big as the box allows, ink bars where needed;
- `width` "An Breite einpassen" / "Fit width": the video is as wide as the viewport; a taller video is cropped at the   top/bottom, a flatter one gets bars above/below;
- `height` "An Höhe einpassen" / "Fit height": the video is as high as the viewport; a wider video is cropped at the   sides, a narrower one gets bars left/right;
- `cover` "Füllen (beschnitten)" / "Fill (cropped)": always fills the viewport, the overflow is cropped. `position` = which part stays when the video is cropped vertically, or where it sits when there are bars above/below. Cropping at the sides always keeps the centre. `viewportObjectFit` turns width/height into contain or cover for a box.

SliceItem.description:
A catalog item (its cut-out icon) placed on a slice, like a text box: position, size, rotation. Language-neutral geometry (the same in every locale file, like the text boxes' rects).

What a tap does is the creator's choice (`action`, default `none`):
- `none`: just an image on the slice;
- `pickup`: the reader takes it – the VN item bridge (`add <item> <qty>`: game variable + story grant with a ref per   place, so the catalog's rules apply: grantable, max count, one-time refs); a taken item is gone from the slice   for that reader (game state, synced with the account's progress);
- `events`: runs `events` – the same VN events as a slice's / group's script (showMessage, addChoice → add item …),   like a click trigger whose area is the item.
